osques  partially excavated, including the Friday mosques, among the mosques found) housing sectors, several outdoor spaces, as well as a funeral area.”  “L. Traversi’s text thus testifies to what, in the eyes of the local authorities and the Muslim community of this part of Ifat, constituted the historical and memorial heritage of the region at the end of the 19th century: two ruined cities, one linked to a certain ‘Sharif Ali’ considered at the time as a sultan, son  of Sa’d al-Din, and whose tomb was celebrated, the other to a certain ‘Ras Alis’.”  '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 956, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 887})
